WEBVTT

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.990
Ready...

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:13.970
Go!

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.370
Whoa, this is...

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.750
She's rustier than I thought.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.010
Teio, stay focused until you finish!

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.240
What do you think, Trainer?

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.810
She's still got a lot of work to do.

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:50.780
That said...

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:57.200
I'm happy enough that she's running again.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:21.720
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.720
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.370
Teio, here's your regimen.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:33.210
Episode 11
\hWhat I Feel

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:34.800
Oof! Basic training, basic training, 
and more basic training...

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.710
<b>Tokai Teio 
Special Training Plan!</b>

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.710
<b></b>• Stretching  30 Minutes

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.710
<b></b>• Roadwork  1 Hour

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.710
<b></b>• Rest  15 Minutes

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.710
<b></b>• Ladder Training  20 Sets

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.710
<b></b>• Strength Training  (Push-Ups, Midsection, Back)

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.710
<b></b>• Rest  15 Minutes

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.710
<b></b>• Tire Pulling 15

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.710
<b></b>• Curls  30 x 6 sets

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.710
It's like I'm getting ready to debut again.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.830
I'm honestly kind of at 
a loss about what to do.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:41.390
But it's times like that—

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:43.100
—you need to focus on the basics.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.350
I'm gonna work hard, like I'm 
starting over from scratch.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:47.600
Teio...

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.890
Plus, I'm already enjoying just 
being able to run on the track again.

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.480
Yeah. Let's work hard together.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.860
Gotta say, though...

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.200
This place is a mess!

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.370
I've been kind of pressed for time lately.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:05.120
Been trying to keep track of the other 
teams, and their noteworthy runners.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.660
A lot of them have grown
a bunch over the summer.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.960
Do you think I can help?

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:12.870
Say what?

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:14.190
It's for the team's sake, right?

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.380
I wanna do what I can to pay 
the others back for their help.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:20.380
Still, I'm not sure I should—

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.550
It'll be fine, just leave it to me!

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.950
I've got a knack for surveillance!

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.480
That's so weird.

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.400
Target confirmed.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.790
What the heck?

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:42.780
So my grandma couldn't 
find her dentures, right?

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:45.390
Winning Ticket...

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:49.250
<b>Notable Accomplishments</b>

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:50.120
<b>• Yayoishou (GII)</b>

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.770
Said to be among the three strongest 
horse girls of the new generation,

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:51.040
<b>1st Place</b>

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:51.040
<b>• Satsuki Sho (GI)</b>

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:51.040
along with Biwa Hayahide 
and Narita Taishin...

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:51.040
<b>4th place</b>

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:51.040
<b>• Tokyo Derby (GI)</b>

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.040
<b>1st Place</b>

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:52.920
After losing in the Satsuki Sho,

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.790
she took the Derby while 
also being ranked most popular.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:59.230
She shows excellent acceleration in the
way she moves up during the final stretch.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:02.800
and her preparations for the Kikkashou 
are looking pitch-perfect.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.240
Lives by the motto, "Be a powerful lady."

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.180
Okay!

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.080
What is she doing?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.270
She's crawling somewhere!

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:19.700
Let's see...

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.530
<b>The Runaway</b>

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.620
Mejiro Palmer.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:26.910
<b>Notable Accomplishments

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.360
Managed to win both Grand Prix races,

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.910
the Takarazuka Kinen and 
Arima Kinen, last year.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.970
Accelerates to full speed early on, 
and at this year's Spring Tennoushou,

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.820
she was able to take the lead early, 
then finish in third place.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:37.470
She sets a crazy pace for everyone else, 
making her a tough cookie to race against.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:42.070
Sucks at hurdle races, and comes 
back from them all banged up.

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:43.220
Okay!

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:49.010
What is that girl even doing?

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.350
Is something the matter, President?

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:52.220
No, not really.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.340
I need you to sign off on these.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.480
Right.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.230
Here we go...

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:03.130
Rice Shower.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:06.950
<b>Notable Accomplishments</b>

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:07.610
<b>• Tokyo Derby (GI)</b>

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.490
After thwarting Mihono 
Bourbon's Triple Crown,

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:08.160
<b>2nd Place</b>

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:08.740
<b>• Kikkasho (GI)</b>

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.740
<b>1st Place</b>

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.740
<b>• Nikkei Sho (GII)</b>

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:09.170
she ended Mejiro McQueen's winning 
streak at the Spring Tennoushou,

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:08.740
<b>1st Place</b>

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.740
<b>• Tennoushou (Spring) (GI)</b>

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:08.740
<b>1st place</b>

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:11.870
demonstrating her strength as a stayer.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:16.150
She was really amazing 
at the Spring Tennoushou!

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:20.090
Oh, I should make a note that 
she eats bread with breakfast.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.130
There we go!

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:27.380
I checked her out already, 
and this one is done, too.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.760
Let's see, let's grab a Shaky-Shaky Jelly,

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.370
the kind that you're supposed 
to shake a bunch...

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.270
What the heck?!

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.960
I ended up accidentally getting the 
1.5 liter soda bottle instead of

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:47.130
the 150 milliliter Shaky-Shaky Jelly!

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.040
Tokai Teio...

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.100
<i>Biwa Hayahide!</i>

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.470
<i>She's been in first or second 
place in every race she's run in.</i>

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:02.040
<i>One of the famous BNW trio.</i>

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.720
I can't!

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:05.130
<i>The way she leaves the competition 
behind during straightaways</i>

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.050
<i>gives her a real champion's aura.</i>

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:09.170
<i>And I have to wonder...</i>

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:12.820
<i>Why is she so intimidating?</i>

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.230
Decarbonated cola, eh?

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:19.480
Very impressive.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:26.100
From the data I've seen, flat soda has 
an incredibly high energy efficiency,

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:29.430
to the point that marathon runners have 
been known to drink it before a race.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:32.200
I would expect nothing less from Tokai Teio.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.510
Uh, I really just...

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:35.200
No need to be modest.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.590
You've got a perfect grasp of nutritional 
theory in addition to your athletic ability.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:42.790
I can see why you were once 
known as the greatest.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:44.590
Sis...

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.210
Yes, I know.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:47.740
My apologies for the interruption.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:51.680
Should we ever race each other, 
try not to be too hard on me.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.690
Never thought you knew Tokai Teio.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:55.750
Guess everybody knows your face, Sis.

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:57.610
Are you saying my face is big?!

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:01.690
Machikane Tannhäuser.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.720
Has plenty of stamina, 
and a knack for long distances.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:08.610
Managed to beat Rice Shower 
at this year's Meguro Kinen.

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:12.410
Nice Nature.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.330
Came in third place at the Arima 
Kinen for two years in a row.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.750
Despite having difficulty 
managing to secure wins,

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:21.290
her reliable running means she's 
consistently on the scoreboard at the end of—

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:22.790
Teio?

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:25.720
Why are you wearing that?

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:27.530
Well, it's...

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.880
You can spy all you want, but try 
to stay out of the way, okay?

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:33.680
You knew?!

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.170
It was kind of obvious in that getup.

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:39.810
Don't just goof off, okay? 
You need to train, too.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.560
I know!

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:45.640
I'm looking forward to seeing 
you race again, too, y'know.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:47.320
Y-You are?

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:51.690
I've had such a hard time 
winning anything lately.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:57.450
I mean, I know that I'm not 
really amazing or anything.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:02.000
But just when I think, 
"Maybe next time," I end up injured.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:07.800
To be honest, I was on the verge of giving 
up when I heard you'd be running again.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:14.430
And when I saw you refuse to give up, 
it made me think I shouldn't, either.

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:16.430
Nature...

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.660
Gosh, what am I getting so sentimental about?

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:21.110
Talk about embarrassing!

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:22.810
Forget I said anything, okay?!

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:26.440
I'm only back because of everyone else.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:29.830
A lot of people have managed 
to show me how they feel.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:36.830
Well, be sure to tell them how <i>you</i> feel.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.580
Just like I did, okay?

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:40.680
Thanks again, Teio!

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:44.100
Thanks, huh...

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:48.210
Turbo, Turbo, Turbo!

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:51.740
If you think you can beat Turbo...

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.820
Tokai Teio!

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:56.080
Hey, race me!

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:56.970
Maybe next time,

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.720
Master Twin Turbo!

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:01.730
She remembered my name.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:03.340
Wait, Master?

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.840
<i>Be sure to tell them how </i>you<i> feel.</i>

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:12.240
Thank you! Thank you!

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.260
Here I am!

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:17.240
<b>Spica</b>

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:17.240
And I got plenty of candid shots.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.160
Let's take a look...

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.470
<b>Horse girl registered with Team Canopus.
Placed third place two years in a row at
the Arima Kinen. Has had trouble winning
a race in the GI, but her reliable racing
 consistently puts her onto the scoreboard,
and can't be underestimated. Has the most
 common sense of anyone on Canopus.</b>

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.470
<b>Avec Dream

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:23.910
<b>Machikane Tannhäuser
A horse girl who specializes in middle
and long distance races affiliated with
Team Canopus. Has yet to win a GI race
but came in third place at the Kikkasho (GI).
Has previously won against the 
Kikkashou-winning Rice Shower.</b>

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:23.910
<b>Rice Shower
Known as the Ebon Stayer. Has won,
and even set records at,
long-distance races like 
the Kikkashou (GI) and Tennoushou (GI)...</b>

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:23.910
These are... candid?

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:25.370
Hey, Trainer.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:27.310
Thanks.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.030
Whoa, what got into you?

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:32.760
You're the one helping me. I oughta—

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.310
It's how I feel about all your help.

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:36.050
Let's keep working hard together!

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:38.870
Yeah, you bet.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:41.120
Teio?

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.310
I see you're back.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:45.810
Excellent work on your mission, Teio-san!

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.940
What's got you looking so serious?

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.440
Guys... thank you.

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:59.450
When I went up on stage... I was able to 
get over some things thanks to you all.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:00.930
Took you long enough—

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:03.580
Thank you, Gold Ship.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.220
You too, Spe-chan.

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:07.370
Oh, it was nothing!

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:09.780
You too, Vodka, Scarlet.

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:11.980
Well, when you go to the trouble 
of saying it out loud...

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:13.250
It's kind of embarrassing.

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:18.370
That really hurt...

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:22.340
<i>Okay! That just leaves McQueen!</i>

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:29.270
McQueen! Hey!

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.920
Teio?

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.870
Working late, I see!

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:34.270
Did you need something?

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:36.900
I just wanted to talk to you.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:39.930
I understand.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:43.410
You were a spy?

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.040
I sure was!

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.160
I was all lurking in the shadows and stuff!

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.940
I would've liked to have seen that.

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:52.520
Also, there's something else, McQueen...

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:54.260
What is it?

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:57.080
For the other day... or really, 
more like, all the time...

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:59.170
I wanted to say tha—

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:01.680
Tha?

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:02.890
Tha...

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:07.430
Teio? Is something the matter?

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:10.440
<i>Huh. That's weird.</i>

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:14.910
Teio? "Tha" what, Teio?

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:14.010
<i>I was able to say it so 
easily to the others.</i>

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.000
<i>Why not her?</i>

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:17.000
Teio?

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:22.320
W-Well...

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:24.320
Um...

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:29.400
You're acting like someone 
about to confess their love.

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:30.600
I am?!

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.680
I'm joking, of course.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:37.710
U-Uh, I just remembered something I need to do!

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:38.730
See ya!

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:39.670
Teio?

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.760
<i>Argh, what is going on?!</i>

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.180
<i>I just wanted to say thank you!</i>

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:48.010
<i>What is wrong with me?!</i>

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:52.020
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:52.020
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:57.430
I didn't get any sleep last night.

00:11:57.430 --> 00:11:58.260
Teio?

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:00.680
M-McQueen!

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:04.030
What's the matter? You seem rather tired.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:06.670
I was up thinking last night.

00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:10.890
Is something bothering you? 
You've been acting strange since yesterday.

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:12.690
Nothing, really!

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.990
You don't seem to have a fever.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:22.670
O-Of course not! Why would I?!

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:26.400
<i>I'm just making this harder 
on myself by overthinking it.</i>

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:29.160
<i>I just need to come out and say it! Normally!</i>

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.190
McQueen!

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:32.060
Yes?

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:34.210
Th-Tha... Tha...

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:39.600
Uh, tha... than... um, tha...

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:42.940
Oh, dear, that's the bell! We should hurry!

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:48.450
<b>• Arima Kinen</b>

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:48.450
<b>• Takarazuka Kinen</b>

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:49.700
The two races where entrants are 
decided by popular ballot are the

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.950
Takarazuka Kinen and Arima Kinen.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:51.400
<i>Why her?</i>

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:55.920
<i>Why is it that, with McQueen, I get so nervous?</i>

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:56.960
Twin Turbo-san!

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:02.470
<i>And she's the last member of 
Spica that I haven't thanked.</i>

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:04.390
<i>At this rate...</i>

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:12.470
<b>Thank you</b>

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:07.920
May I...

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:08.530
Hell no.

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:10.840
This thanks is for me.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:12.470
Could I...

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.520
You can't have it.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:15.190
You can't have it!

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:19.690
Boo-hoo-hoo...

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:22.310
You don't have to get so mad, Spe-chan!

00:13:22.310 --> 00:13:23.820
I don't have to what, now?

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:26.960
Spe-chan!

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:32.090
You're having trouble telling 
someone how you feel?

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:35.100
I was wondering if there 
was a trick I could use.

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:37.960
Good question. If it was me...

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:41.580
I would put my feelings into a snack, 
using the language of snacks!

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:43.070
There's a language of those?

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:43.850
Yes!

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:47.560
For example, baumkuchen represents 
a desire for continued happiness!

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:49.980
Tiramisu is a way of asking 
for someone to cheer you up.

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:52.880
Carrot pancakes represent feeling full!

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:55.360
Carrot-stuffed mochi represents free seconds.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:57.480
And this is something you learned, Spe-chan?

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.600
I did! But opinions vary!

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:03.830
I think the idea of a 
present might work, though.

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:09.490
Look at this, Teio-san!

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:12.480
It's a premium carrot with a honey glaze!

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.870
I think this is supposed to represent...

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:17.500
<b>Carrot</b>

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:17.500
We're not shopping for you, Spe-chan!

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:22.380
Would a snack really work, 
like Spe-chan thinks?

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:25.380
Teio-san!

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.880
Kita-chan? And Dia-chan's with you.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:31.900
Wait... huh? What's with the outfits?

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:35.020
Trick or treat!

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:36.690
Oh, Halloween!

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:38.140
Yes, that's right!

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:40.310
You better give us a treat...

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:42.020
Or we'll play a trick on you!

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.310
You two look so cute!

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:45.540
Yay!

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:46.890
Is it okay if I take a picture?

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:47.860
Sure!

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:48.780
Please!

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:50.920
Let's see...

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.490
<b>Good Luck</b>

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.320
Okay, say cheeseburger!

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:58.530
Teio-san, is that...

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:03.640
I'm counting on the charm you made 
me to help keep me going, okay?

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:06.850
Okay! I'll always be rooting for you!

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:07.630
Right.

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:09.360
And thanks again.

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:17.390
Funny, I don't have any trouble 
saying it to Kita-chan.

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:22.770
Well, I've been meaning to 
say thank you to McQueen,

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:24.650
but it's been hard for some reason.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.080
Do you know what I mean?

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:28.710
Can't you just tell her?

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:31.240
Well, you're right, but...

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:34.690
Okay, why don't you try 
saying it to Dia-chan?

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:37.370
Just an "I appreciate everything 
you do for me" kind of thing.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.450
Oh, that'll be easy!

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:41.120
This should be fun!

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.460
Dia-chan!

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:44.880
Yes, go ahead.

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:47.010
Well...

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:47.800
Yes?

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:54.450
Um... thank you for always 
being with me and...

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.100
Well...

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.240
It's like you're confessing 
your love or something!

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:02.190
You're blushing bright red, Kita-chan!

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:05.650
Aw, quit teasing me!

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:10.500
I guess the closer you are to someone, 
the more embarrassing it is.

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:14.530
I always get embarrassed talking 
to my mom on Mother's Day.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:18.560
Kita-chan, what do you think about me?

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:19.660
What do you mean?!

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.360
You're my rival, and my best friend, and...

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:26.170
I care about you a lot!

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:32.850
Th-This is even more embarrassing, Kita-chan!

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:36.820
I get it now.

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:41.620
<i>That's right. It's simpler than I figured.</i>

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.210
<i>To me, McQueen is...</i>

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.320
<b>Mejiro McQueen-sama</b>

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.320
<b>This is an invitation to a date ♥</b>

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.320
<b>I'll be waiting for you in front 
\hof Tracen Academy tomorrow at 11 AM!</b>

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.320
<b>Don't miss it!</b>

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.320
<b>From Tokai Teio</b>

00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:08.590
Teio!

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:19.410
I'm sorry, it took a moment 
to figure out this costume.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:22.240
And I've never worn it before, 
so I'm not sure about how it looks.

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:23.430
It's okay!

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.690
You look great!

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:29.160
That's a relief to hear.

00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:33.360
All right, let's get this 
Halloween date on the road!

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.830
<b>Miyazaki-Sourced Chicken</b>

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.830
<b>Takoyaki</b>

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.400
What brought this on all of a sudden?

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:50.840
Well, I figured you'd like a celebration 
that involved a lot of sweets.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.520
D-Don't be ridiculous!

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:54.670
I've actually been cutting back lately.

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:03.970
I think they're selling crepes over there.

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:05.330
They are?!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.040
I mean, clearly they are.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:11.620
Let's check everything out! Come on!

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:12.860
Right.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:16.620
Here you are!

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:18.860
Thank you!

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:18.860
<b>Balloons</b>

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:23.870
You can do it, McQueen!

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:27.870
<b>Cotton Candy</b>

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:32.130
That's not how that works!

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.380
I can't hit it...

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:39.230
Leave it to me.

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:40.300
Okay!

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:42.720
That's not how that works.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:46.020
That is also not how that works.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.770
<b>If you can finish it in
1 minute, it's free</b>

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.770
<b>J
u
m
b
o</b>

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.770
<b>B
o
b
